.TH SAPHIRA-INSTALL-PLAN 5 "Saphira Linux" "Installation plan format"
.SH NAME
saphira-install-plan \- declarative installation manifest format
.SH DESCRIPTION
An installation manifest is one strict
.B KEY=VALUE
file describing firmware, init system, root filesystem, storage
layout, role, repository and identity for a Saphira installation.
.BR saphira-install-plan (8)
validates it and prints the human-readable plan; the USB installer,
the future UEFI pre-boot menu and
.BR saphira-image (8)
all consume the same format, so one file describes an installation
everywhere.
.PP
The format is deliberately EFI-parseable: bare words, no quoting, no
shell syntax, one pair per line,
.B #
comments and blanks allowed. Unknown keys are
.B refused
(a typo must fail validation, never install the wrong system), and
.B credentials never belong in a manifest
(firstboot sets passwords on the installed machine's own console;
any key naming a password, secret, token or private key is refused).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B PLAN_VERSION
Must be
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B FIRMWARE
.BR bios ,
.BR uefi
or
.BR auto
(autodetect at install time; both the BIOS boot partition and the ESP
are written).
.TP
.B INIT
.B openrc
(Saphira) or
.B systemd
(SaphiraD).
.TP
.B ROOTFS
.BR ext4 ,
.BR xfs
or
.BR zfs .
Btrfs is a supported kernel filesystem but is never an offered root.
.TP
.B LAYOUT
.BR direct ,
.BR lvm
or
.BR zpool .
.B zpool
requires
.B ROOTFS=zfs
(and vice versa: a pool is not a partition);
.B lvm
requires ext4 or XFS.
.TP
.B DISK
Target device path
.RB ( /dev/... ).
The planner never touches it; the installer UI confirms destruction.
.TP
.B ROLE
.BR base ,
.BR docker ,
.BR k8s-control ,
.BR k8s-worker ,
.BR openstack-controller ,
.BR openstack-compute
or
.BR openstack-storage .
Roles select package profiles and firstboot/role setup; single-service
appliance roles arrive later and follow the same key.
.TP
.B PROFILE
Package profile name resolvable in the profile tree
.RB ( SAPHIRA_PROFILE_ROOT ,
default
.IR /usr/share/saphira/profiles ).
Profiles describe package intentions only, never disk or network.
.TP
.B REPOSITORY
.B https://
package URL.
.TP
.B HOSTNAME
Machine hostname (letters, digits, hyphens; set at assembly, honoured
by firstboot).
.TP
.B POOL , DATASET , BOOT_SIZE
ZFS only.
.B POOL
defaults by convention to
.BR tank ;
.B DATASET
must live under it
.RB ( tank/ROOTS/saphira ,
.IR tank/ROOTS/saphirad ,
...);
.B BOOT_SIZE
(e.g.
.BR 1G )
sizes the separate ext4
.B /boot
partition GRUB reads, so GRUB never needs to understand pool
features. The remainder of the disk is a ZFS partition owned by the
pool; the initramfs imports the pool and mounts the dataset at
.BR / .
.TP
.B VG , LV_SIZE
LVM only.
.B VG
names the volume group;
.B LV_SIZE
(e.g.
.B 20G
or
.B %FREE
) sizes the root logical volume. The installer initramfs activates
the group before mounting.
.SH KERNEL SUPPORT
ext4/XFS availability is provable from a kernel
.IR .config :
.B --kernel-config
points at one and validation fails closed when the filesystem symbol
is not
.BR =y .
ZFS rides out-of-tree kernel modules no
.I .config
can prove; it is always reported as a
.B needs:
line the installer environment must honour (kmod present in the
installer and the target, import hook in the initramfs).
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/saphira/install-manifest.example
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-install-plan (8),
.BR saphira-profiles (5),
.BR saphira-install (8)
